1
00:00:00,079 --> 00:00:01,939
The cabin lights go down before a night landing,

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:04,239
and it reads as mood lighting or saving power.

3
00:00:04,519 --> 00:00:05,119
It is neither.

4
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:07,419
Eyes take several minutes to adapt to darkness,

5
00:00:07,719 --> 00:00:09,760
and takeoff and landing are when an evacuation

6
00:00:09,819 --> 00:00:10,920
is most likely to be needed.

7
00:00:11,239 --> 00:00:13,179
If the cabin were brightly lit and the power

8
00:00:13,259 --> 00:00:15,039
went, everyone aboard would be effectively

9
00:00:15,079 --> 00:00:16,699
blind at the worst possible moment.

10
00:00:17,020 --> 00:00:19,159
Dimming early means your eyes are already adjusted,

11
00:00:19,539 --> 00:00:21,840
and the floor path lighting reads clearly instead

12
00:00:21,879 --> 00:00:22,500
of washing out.

13
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:24,119
The lights go down so you can see.
